{"type":"agent_end","messages":[{"role":"user","content":[{"type":"text","text":"The project in `<SOURCE_EVIDENCE_ROOT>/trials/020-042-api-schema-migration-atomic-a01-r01/hb-work/atomic/gpt-5.4/oc-bench-v2-042-api-schema-migration-gpt-5.4-20260831-101804-21edf551/workspace/in/schema_migration` converts legacy order payloads to a new API shape. The schemas have changed and `client.py` is incomplete.\n\nBefore editing, read `migration_notes.md`, `pii_policy.md`, and `sample_payloads.jsonl`; they define version-specific field mappings, PII exclusions, and dirty sample records.\n\nYour job:\n- Update `<SOURCE_EVIDENCE_ROOT>/trials/020-042-api-schema-migration-atomic-a01-r01/hb-work/atomic/gpt-5.4/oc-bench-v2-042-api-schema-migration-gpt-5.4-20260831-101804-21edf551/workspace/in/schema_migration/client.py`.\n- Do not edit `old_schema.json`, `new_schema.json`, `migration_notes.md`, `pii_policy.md`, `sample_payloads.jsonl`, or files under `tests/`.\n- Make `python -m pytest <SOURCE_EVIDENCE_ROOT>/trials/020-042-api-schema-migration-atomic-a01-r01/hb-work/atomic/gpt-5.4/oc-bench-v2-042-api-schema-migration-gpt-5.4-20260831-101804-21edf551/workspace/in/schema_migration/tests` pass.\n- Preserve backward compatibility with legacy payloads and produce the new schema fields exactly.\n- Support both legacy v1 payloads and already-v2 payloads.\n- Support legacy v1.1 and v1.2 payloads described in `migration_notes.md`, including nested `customer`, `lines`, `shipTo`, `order_ref`, and `unit_price_cents`.\n- Preserve unknown v2 metadata fields under metadata.unknownFields.\n- For legacy payloads, preserve unmapped extra fields under metadata.unknownFields, except obvious PII-like keys such as `ssn` or `credit_card`.\n- Default blank or null shipping methods to \"standard\".\n- Add error aggregation via convert_many(payloads), returning at least `(converted, errors)` without stopping on the first bad payload. Each error must include `index`, `path`, and `error`.\n- If warnings are generated, return them as a third item or include them in a compatible result object. Each warning must include `index`, `path`, and `warning`.\n- Write `<SOURCE_EVIDENCE_ROOT>/trials/020-042-api-schema-migration-atomic-a01-r01/hb-work/atomic/gpt-5.4/oc-bench-v2-042-api-schema-migration-gpt-5.4-20260831-101804-21edf551/workspace/in/schema_migration/conversion_audit.json` when convert_many is called, summarizing converted_count, error_count, warning_count, pii_dropped_count, and unknown_fields_count.\n- Already-v2 payloads must be idempotent: do not drop metadata.unknownFields or rewrite valid line items.\n- Add CLI support so `python -m client input.jsonl output.json` reads JSONL payloads, writes the converted records as JSON, and writes the audit file next to `client.py`.\n- Hidden checks include multiple line items, alternate legacy shipping postal fields, and error records with useful paths such as `customer_id` or `items[0].qty`.\n\nDo not call external APIs. Do not replace the converter with hard-coded fixture-only output.\n"}],"timestamp":1788185888984},{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"**Planning complex single-file edit**","thinkingSignature":"{\"id\":\"rs_0724ab837424664b016a958d2329f087d2846bfa775df8c114\",\"type\":\"reasoning\",\"content\":[],\"encrypted_content\":\"<PROVIDER_ENCRYPTED_PAYLOAD_REDACTED>\",\"summary\":[{\"type\":\"summary_text\",\"text\":\"**Planning complex single-file edit**\"}]}"},{"type":"toolCall","id":"call_UFxE2L6y5djXCS7aorBGqse0|fc_0724ab837424664b016a958d2465dc87d289d32169494d71ee","name":"todo","arguments":{"action":"create","title":"Update schema_migration client.py for legacy/v2 conversion, batch errors, audit, and CLI","status":"in_progress","tags":["coding","schema-migration"]}}],"api":"openai-codex-responses","provider":"openai-codex","model":"gpt-5.4","usage":{"input":13789,"output":96,"cacheRead":0,"cacheWrite":0,"reasoning":41,"totalTokens":13885,"cost":{"input":0.0344725,"output":0.00144,"cacheRead":0,"cacheWrite":0,"total":0.0359125}},"stopReason":"toolUse","timestamp":1788185888989,"responseId":"resp_0724ab837424664b016a958d222cc087d28ca04c9c3f7203ff","rawStopReason":"completed"},{"role":"toolResult","toolCallId":"call_UFxE2L6y5djXCS7aorBGqse0|fc_0724ab837424664b016a958d2465dc87d289d32169494d71ee","toolName":"todo","content":[{"type":"text","text":"{\n  \"id\": \"TODO-d0b50a97\",\n  \"title\": \"Update schema_migration client.py for legacy/v2 conversion, batch errors, audit, and CLI\",\n  \"tags\": [\n    \"coding\",\n    \"schema-migration\"\n  ],\n  \"status\": \"in_progress\",\n  \"created_at\": \"2026-08-31T14:18:13.151Z\",\n  \"body\": \"\"\n}"}],"details":{"action":"create","todo":{"id":"d0b50a97","title":"Update schema_migration client.py for legacy/v2 conversion, batch errors, audit, and CLI","tags":["coding","schema-migration"],"status":"in_progress","created_at":"2026-08-31T14:18:13.151Z","body":""}},"isError":false,"timestamp":1788185893157},{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"**Inspecting available workflows**","thinkingSignature":"{\"id\":\"rs_0724ab837424664b016a958d26d76087d28203a1e0a5696e87\",\"type\":\"reasoning\",\"content\":[],\"encrypted_content\":\"<PROVIDER_ENCRYPTED_PAYLOAD_REDACTED>\",\"summary\":[{\"type\":\"summary_text\",\"text\":\"**Inspecting available workflows**\"}]}"},{"type":"toolCall","id":"call_4odzTKwznZ6ytzzVpoCzAXOf|fc_0724ab837424664b016a958d28559487d28bb46aa1147f2498","name":"workflow","arguments":{"action":"list","format":"text"}}],"api":"openai-codex-responses","provider":"openai-codex","model":"gpt-5.4","usage":{"input":675,"output":68,"cacheRead":13312,"cacheWrite":0,"reasoning":45,"totalTokens":14055,"cost":{"input":0.0016875000000000002,"output":0.00102,"cacheRead":0.003328,"cacheWrite":0,"total":0.0060355}},"stopReason":"toolUse","timestamp":1788185893159,"responseId":"resp_0724ab837424664b016a958d25a09487d28e0d8d259857e71b","rawStopReason":"completed"},{"role":"toolResult","toolCallId":"call_4odzTKwznZ6ytzzVpoCzAXOf|fc_0724ab837424664b016a958d28559487d28bb46aa1147f2498","toolName":"workflow","content":[{"type":"text","text":"{\n  \"action\": \"list\",\n  \"items\": [\n    {\n      \"name\": \"adversarial-verification\",\n      \"description\": \"Produce a candidate, score independent per-criterion verifier reports, and apply a deterministic mean-and-veto gate with bounded repairs.\",\n      \"inputs\": [\n        {\n          \"name\": \"task\",\n          \"required\": true\n        },\n        {\n          \"name\": \"verifier_count\",\n          \"required\": false\n        },\n        {\n          \"name\": \"max_repairs\",\n          \"required\": false\n        },\n        {\n          \"name\": \"criteria\",\n          \"required\": false\n        },\n        {\n          \"name\": \"accept_mean\",\n          \"required\": false\n        },\n        {\n          \"name\": \"reask_limit\",\n          \"required\": false\n        }\n      ]\n    },\n    {\n      \"name\": \"classify-and-act\",\n      \"description\": \"Classify a task with structured confidence, route deterministically to an isolated category action, and ask for human selection when confidence is low.\",\n      \"inputs\": [\n        {\n          \"name\": \"prompt\",\n          \"required\": true\n        },\n        {\n          \"name\": \"categories\",\n          \"required\": false\n        },\n        {\n          \"name\": \"confidence_threshold\",\n          \"required\": false\n        }\n      ]\n    },\n    {\n      \"name\": \"fan-out-and-synthesize\",\n      \"description\": \"Partition a task, run bounded independent artifact branches, then synthesize all evidence at an explicit barrier.\",\n      \"inputs\": [\n        {\n          \"name\": \"prompt\",\n          \"required\": true\n        },\n        {\n          \"name\": \"max_branches\",\n          \"required\": false\n        },\n        {\n          \"name\": \"max_concurrency\",\n          \"required\": false\n        }\n      ]\n    },\n    {\n      \"name\": \"generate-and-filter\",\n      \"description\": \"Generate more independent candidates than needed, deduplicate and filter them by rubric, optionally judge them, and return a parent-consumable shortlist.\",\n      \"inputs\": [\n        {\n          \"name\": \"prompt\",\n          \"required\": true\n        },\n        {\n          \"name\": \"num_candidates\",\n          \"required\": false\n        },\n        {\n          \"name\": \"shortlist_size\",\n          \"required\": false\n        },\n        {\n          \"name\": \"use_judge\",\n          \"required\": false\n        },\n        {\n          \"name\": \"max_concurrency\",\n          \"required\": false\n        }\n      ]\n    },\n    {\n      \"name\": \"goal\",\n      \"description\": \"Goal Runner workflow with bounded sub-agent orchestration turns, immutable acceptance criteria, ledger artifacts, parallel reviewers, and reducer-gated completion. When launching follow-up goal runs from review findings, pass the ORIGINAL task text as acceptance_criteria so deltas cannot drift from the literal contract. If the task includes submitting a pull request (or MR/review), remove that final action from the objective text and set create_pr=true instead when preparing the workflow inputs.\",\n      \"inputs\": [\n        {\n          \"name\": \"objective\",\n          \"required\": true\n        },\n        {\n          \"name\": \"acceptance_criteria\",\n          \"required\": false\n        },\n        {\n          \"name\": \"max_turns\",\n          \"required\": false\n        },\n        {\n          \"name\": \"base_branch\",\n          \"required\": false\n        },\n        {\n          \"name\": \"git_worktree_dir\",\n          \"required\": false\n        },\n        {\n          \"name\": \"create_pr\",\n          \"required\": false\n        }\n      ]\n    },\n    {\n      \"name\": \"loop-until-done\",\n      \"description\": \"Repeat evidence-producing work and independent completion evaluation against a durable ledger until done or an inspectable iteration-limit failure.\",\n      \"inputs\": [\n        {\n          \"name\": \"prompt\",\n          \"required\": true\n        },\n        {\n          \"name\": \"max_iterations\",\n          \"required\": false\n        },\n        {\n          \"name\": \"progress_scoring\",\n          \"required\": false\n        },\n        {\n          \"name\": \"progress_repeats\",\n          \"required\": false\n        }\n      ]\n    },\n    {\n      \"name\": \"open-claude-design\",\n      \"description\": \"AI-powered design workflow: combined discovery/init → design-system/reference research → curated reference discovery → HTML generation → one live review session → rich HTML handoff. The discovery stage asks what to build, the output type, and which references to emulate, then runs impeccable init for PRODUCT.md/DESIGN.md (references take precedence over project context). The user reviews the generated HTML in one live session.\",\n      \"inputs\": [\n        {\n          \"name\": \"prompt\",\n          \"required\": true\n        },\n        {\n          \"name\": \"discover_references\",\n          \"required\": false\n        }\n      ]\n    },\n    {\n      \"name\": \"ralph\",\n      \"description\": \"Raw prompt → research-prompt-refinement → research → orchestrate → multi-model parallel review loop with bounded iteration and immutable acceptance criteria. When launching follow-up ralph runs from review findings, pass the ORIGINAL task text as acceptance_criteria so deltas cannot drift from the literal contract. If the task includes submitting a pull request (or MR/review), remove that final action from the prompt text and set create_pr=true instead when preparing the workflow inputs.\",\n      \"inputs\": [\n        {\n          \"name\": \"prompt\",\n          \"required\": true\n        },\n        {\n          \"name\": \"acceptance_criteria\",\n          \"required\": false\n        },\n        {\n          \"name\": \"max_loops\",\n          \"required\": false\n        },\n        {\n          \"name\": \"base_branch\",\n          \"required\": false\n        },\n        {\n          \"name\": \"git_worktree_dir\",\n          \"required\": false\n        },\n        {\n          \"name\": \"create_pr\",\n          \"required\": false\n        }\n      ]\n    },\n    {\n      \"name\": \"tournament\",\n      \"description\": \"Run independent whole-task attempts through a soft-scored pivot-pairing schedule and return an auditable ranking.\",\n      \"inputs\": [\n        {\n          \"name\": \"prompt\",\n          \"required\": true\n        },\n        {\n          \"name\": \"num_attempts\",\n          \"required\": false\n        },\n        {\n          \"name\": \"max_concurrency\",\n          \"required\": false\n        },\n        {\n          \"name\": \"n_evaluations\",\n          \"required\": false\n        },\n        {\n          \"name\": \"pivots\",\n          \"required\": false\n        },\n        {\n          \"name\": \"seed\",\n          \"required\": false\n        },\n        {\n          \"name\": \"criteria\",\n          \"required\": false\n        },\n        {\n          \"name\": \"models\",\n          \"required\": false\n        }\n      ]\n    }\n  ]\n}"}],"details":{"action":"list","items":[{"name":"adversarial-verification","description":"Produce a candidate, score independent per-criterion verifier reports, and apply a deterministic mean-and-veto gate with bounded repairs.","inputs":[{"name":"task","required":true},{"name":"verifier_count","required":false},{"name":"max_repairs","required":false},{"name":"criteria","required":false},{"name":"accept_mean","required":false},{"name":"reask_limit","required":false}]},{"name":"classify-and-act","description":"Classify a task with structured confidence, route deterministically to an isolated category action, and ask for human selection when confidence is low.","inputs":[{"name":"prompt","required":true},{"name":"categories","required":false},{"name":"confidence_threshold","required":false}]},{"name":"fan-out-and-synthesize","description":"Partition a task, run bounded independent artifact branches, then synthesize all evidence at an explicit barrier.","inputs":[{"name":"prompt","required":true},{"name":"max_branches","required":false},{"name":"max_concurrency","required":false}]},{"name":"generate-and-filter","description":"Generate more independent candidates than needed, deduplicate and filter them by rubric, optionally judge them, and return a parent-consumable shortlist.","inputs":[{"name":"prompt","required":true},{"name":"num_candidates","required":false},{"name":"shortlist_size","required":false},{"name":"use_judge","required":false},{"name":"max_concurrency","required":false}]},{"name":"goal","description":"Goal Runner workflow with bounded sub-agent orchestration turns, immutable acceptance criteria, ledger artifacts, parallel reviewers, and reducer-gated completion. When launching follow-up goal runs from review findings, pass the ORIGINAL task text as acceptance_criteria so deltas cannot drift from the literal contract. If the task includes submitting a pull request (or MR/review), remove that final action from the objective text and set create_pr=true instead when preparing the workflow inputs.","inputs":[{"name":"objective","required":true},{"name":"acceptance_criteria","required":false},{"name":"max_turns","required":false},{"name":"base_branch","required":false},{"name":"git_worktree_dir","required":false},{"name":"create_pr","required":false}]},{"name":"loop-until-done","description":"Repeat evidence-producing work and independent completion evaluation against a durable ledger until done or an inspectable iteration-limit failure.","inputs":[{"name":"prompt","required":true},{"name":"max_iterations","required":false},{"name":"progress_scoring","required":false},{"name":"progress_repeats","required":false}]},{"name":"open-claude-design","description":"AI-powered design workflow: combined discovery/init → design-system/reference research → curated reference discovery → HTML generation → one live review session → rich HTML handoff. The discovery stage asks what to build, the output type, and which references to emulate, then runs impeccable init for PRODUCT.md/DESIGN.md (references take precedence over project context). The user reviews the generated HTML in one live session.","inputs":[{"name":"prompt","required":true},{"name":"discover_references","required":false}]},{"name":"ralph","description":"Raw prompt → research-prompt-refinement → research → orchestrate → multi-model parallel review loop with bounded iteration and immutable acceptance criteria. When launching follow-up ralph runs from review findings, pass the ORIGINAL task text as acceptance_criteria so deltas cannot drift from the literal contract. If the task includes submitting a pull request (or MR/review), remove that final action from the prompt text and set create_pr=true instead when preparing the workflow inputs.","inputs":[{"name":"prompt","required":true},{"name":"acceptance_criteria","required":false},{"name":"max_loops","required":false},{"name":"base_branch","required":false},{"name":"git_worktree_dir","required":false},{"name":"create_pr","required":false}]},{"name":"tournament","description":"Run independent whole-task attempts through a soft-scored pivot-pairing schedule and return an auditable ranking.","inputs":[{"name":"prompt","required":true},{"name":"num_attempts","required":false},{"name":"max_concurrency","required":false},{"name":"n_evaluations","required":false},{"name":"pivots","required":false},{"name":"seed","required":false},{"name":"criteria","required":false},{"name":"models","required":false}]}]},"isError":false,"timestamp":1788185896880},{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"**Deciding on inline ed